{"author":"schacon@gmail.com","body":"## Updated Design: Git Meta Key/Value Storage\n\nWriteups stored as git-meta key/values, no separate ref needed.\n\n### Key Structure\n\nticgit:writeups:<uuid>:title    = \"rethink sync protocol\"\nticgit:writeups:<uuid>:authors  = [\"alice\", \"bob\"]\nticgit:writeups:<uuid>:versions = [<version1>, <version2>, ...]\n\n### Version Format\n\nEach version in the list is a markdown document with optional YAML frontmatter:\n\n---\nauthor: alice\ndate: 2026-05-12T13:40:00Z\n---\n\nHere is my thinking on the sync protocol redesign...\n\n### How it works\n\n- ti writeup new --title \"...\" — generates UUID, sets title key, adds creator to authors, appends first version\n- ti writeup edit <id> — opens editor, appends new version with current user as author, adds to authors list if not there\n- ti writeup show <id> — reads title, authors, shows latest version (or --all for full history)\n- ti writeup list — iterates ticgit:writeups:*:title keys\n- ti writeup promote <id> — creates ticket from latest version content\n\n### Benefits\n\n- Native git-meta storage, no special refs or directory structure\n- Multi-user: each edit appends a version, authors list tracks contributors\n- Versions are self-describing via frontmatter (author, date, optional tags)\n- Syncs automatically with ti sync since it is just git-meta data\n- Clean namespace under ticgit:writeups:"}